  "report_markdown": "DRAFT\n\n**Complaint/History**\n- Diarrhea for the last three days, described as loose and watery stools, occurring 6–7 times per day.\n- Associated lower abdominal pain, localized to the left side, described as cramp-like, intermittent, and non-radiating.\n- Vomiting at the onset of symptoms, now resolved; vomit was food-colored with no blood.\n- Feverish sensation at symptom onset (3–4 days ago), but no measured temperature; no current fever.\n- Weakness, shakiness, and loss of appetite.\n- Able to tolerate fluids, soups, and smoothies.\n- Symptoms began after eating at a Chinese restaurant four days ago.\n- One child had vomiting but no diarrhea; no other household members affected.\n- Symptoms impacting daily activities, including need to stay close to the toilet; patient has continued going to work (accountant).\n\n**Relevant Background**\n- Asthma, well-controlled on inhaler.\n- No other chronic bowel or gastrointestinal conditions reported.\n\n**Medications**\n- Inhaler for asthma.\n- No other medications.\n\n**Allergies**\n- Not documented.\n\n**Findings**\n- Left lower abdominal pain, cramp-like, intermittent.\n- No blood in stool or vomit.\n- No current fever, but subjective fever at onset.\n- No sweating reported.\n- No travel history, smoking, or alcohol use.\n\n**Clinician's Assessment**\n- Likely acute gastroenteritis, possibly post-food ingestion (Chinese takeaway).\n- Viral etiology suspected; bacterial cause not ruled out.\n\n**Plan/Follow-up**\n- Conservative management: oral rehydration (e.g., Dioralyte), continued fluid intake.\n- Paracetamol 2 tablets up to 4 times daily for fever and discomfort in the first few days.\n- Advised to take 2–3 days off work and rest.\n- Return for review if symptoms persist beyond 3–4 days; stool sample may be required if no improvement.\n- No antibiotics prescribed at this stage.\n- Treatment plan discussed and understood; no questions from patient.",
